  "reason": "The occurrence 'myelin in the peripheral nervous system' refers specifically to myelin formed by Schwann cells. While 'myelin around axons' is an existing concept defined as being formed by Oligodendrocytes in the CNS, the biological entity (Schwann cell vs. Oligodendrocyte) and location (PNS vs. CNS) differ significantly. Therefore, they are distinct concepts rather than aliases."
